### Key Features Implemented
- All animations are standalone HTML files (no external dependencies)
- All animations support `prefers-reduced-motion` accessibility
- All animations have click-to-restart functionality
- Smooth 60fps performance on modern browsers
- Clean, maintainable code with consistent patterns
- Professional visual quality with gradients, shadows, filters

### Technical Achievements
- 10 unique animation techniques demonstrated
- Mix of SVG path animation, Canvas rendering, CSS transforms
- Advanced effects: metaballs, glitch, 3D transforms, morphing
- Proper easing functions for natural motion
- Efficient rendering with requestAnimationFrame
- Accessibility-first design

## Commits
1. Foundation: project structure, logo design, first animations
2. Particles and morphing animations (techniques 2-3)
3. Glitch and liquid animations (techniques 4-5)
4. Kinetic, 3D, reveal, wave, typewriter (techniques 6-10)
5. Gallery index and comprehensive README

## Retrospective

### What Went Well
- Clean, systematic implementation of all 10 techniques
- Consistent code patterns across all animations
- Strong accessibility support (reduced-motion)
- No external dependencies - truly standalone files
- Professional visual quality achieved
- Comprehensive documentation created

### Technical Highlights
- Liquid animations using SVG goo filter
- Particle systems with proper physics
- Smooth path morphing with interpolation
- RGB channel separation for glitch effects
- 3D transforms with proper perspective

### Challenges Overcome
- Morphing animations required careful path normalization
- Particle effects needed optimization for performance
- Liquid effects balanced visual quality vs. performance
- Glitch effects required multiple layered techniques

### Code Quality
- Consistent naming conventions
- Reusable easing functions
- Clear separation of concerns
- Well-commented complex sections
- No hardcoded values where avoidable

